{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the diff from 7d74234c at head 117100611d1a8fb4cc194f1fd1f7fdf05f54a37f, tree 32947a56, for request 4f3336c1 under rulings 90ee0518 and 46552b89, and review request bb7427a5. Verdict: APPROVED.\n\nRuling 46552b89 scopes this review to the diff from 7d74234c and the new gate. The diff changes four paths: `packages/scope/src/diag.ts`, its existing `packages/scope/test/redaction.test.ts`, the note and the manifest. It touches no lineage or authority code, so the lineage conclusions of 61a8c0ce carry over. Correction b1ba4dde withdraws that review's allowlist claim for a stateful name, and this review closes it.\n\n## The repair\n\n- `diagnosis` now reads `thrown.name` once, checks that value against `SAFE_NAMES` and returns the same value. Any other value gives `Error`. A throwing getter still lands in the existing catch and gives `object`.\n- A report now keeps only an allowlisted word for the error name, including for a stateful getter. `SAFE_NAMES.has` compares by identity, so an object can't pass. The other parts of the diagnosis are unchanged.\n- The test adds a getter that returns `Error` on the first read and private text after that, in the existing case. No other assertion changes. The note's control restores the old expression and gets one named assertion failure. I checked the control's receipt digest and did not rerun it.\n\n## Gate and evidence\n\n- The new full gate at 4aa254e9, tree ba5bcec8, closed 0/0 with complete capture and matching source after the run. Its `test.log` shows Node 84, Counting 56, Plain 3,193 with one skip and Native 888 with two skips.\n- From 4aa254e9 to this head, only the note and the manifest change, so the documents-only rule applies and no new gate is due.\n- The evidence verifies. All 209 manifest rows that carry a path and digest match. The four collections have 303, 280, 92 and 305 files, each `SHA256SUMS` reruns clean, and no file is writable. Earlier failures stay at their own checkpoints.\n- The 16 artifacts match the 16 paths that differ from main. `git merge-tree --write-tree` onto main 23865f98 gives tree 32947a56.\n- I ran these once each:\n  - `redaction.test.ts` passes 2 of 2;\n  - `check-notes` gives 0 warnings;\n  - `check-commit-messages` checks 10 with 0 flagged;\n  - `check-doc-links` on an export finds 774 links with 0 broken;\n  - `git diff --check` is clean.\n- The worktree stayed clean.\n\n## For the planner\n\nThe two points in 61a8c0ce still apply. This head opens every WorkspaceHost provider path on real rooms, and the J4 successor packet and the third S1 room are the first live runs of those paths. A lineage refusal says only that the reader returned null, and it doesn't name the guard.\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe repair stays inside the existing diagnosis function, and the design doesn't change. Approved.\n\n## Security\n\nThe allowlist now holds for every thrown value that I can construct, and the diff adds no route, pin or authority check. Together with 61a8c0ce, the repair and the diagnosis are approved for local source. Approved.\n\n## Simplification\n\nThe repair adds one local variable and one case's worth of assertions. Approved.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved.\n- Security: approved.\n- Simplification: approved.\n- The request's checks: the repair, the control, Gate 2 and the evidence all hold.\n\nThis approval covers local source only. It claims no hosted or provider success and no cause for the S1 stops. It releases no J4 or S1 action.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3959551433bd19366b4eecd2c5c7ad0036857ed4","binding":"assigned","head":"117100611d1a8fb4cc194f1fd1f7fdf05f54a37f","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:87f44b02231c41ef48f2f064e170308f5e0340fc\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d38ace314be6c19159fa73b49a3c7755d49ac492\"]","review_frontier":"g